  "findings": [
    "The diffuser loses money on ads: ACOS 45.5% against a 25.0% target and a 37.1% break-even. \"reed diffuser\" (54.9% ACOS, the biggest spender) is cut by the full 30% step, 1.30 to 0.91. At the new bids the product's last 30 days would have run at 35.6%, still above target, so the next weekly run cuts again.",
    "In QM | Candles | SP Exact, top of search sells at 27.0% ACOS and product pages at 50.4%. The top-of-search adjustment goes from 40% to 90% (the formula asks for 161%; one change moves at most 50 points), rest of search from 0% to 40%, and every base bid in the campaign is multiplied by 0.7643 so the placement change moves spend between placements, not the campaign's overall bid level.",
    "2 targets reached at least 2 times their clicks gate with no order and are paused: \"wood wick candle\" (46 clicks, 59.73), \"substitutes\" (88 clicks, 44.27), 104.00 in all.",
    "Candle TACOS is 9.3% against your 10%. With ads at 31.8% of candle sales, that allows a 31.4% ACOS, so the candle targets that beat it are raised: \"candle gift set\" 1.20 to 1.38, close-match 0.90 to 1.08.",
    "Last year's Black Friday to Cyber Monday converted 1.34x your usual rate on 2.12x the daily clicks. The plan raises 4 proven targets by 30.0% on 2026-11-26 and reverts them on 2026-12-01; the auto campaign's budget goes from 60.00 to 166.00 a day. Campaigns still above target keep their budgets."
  ],
  "warnings": [
    "QM-WAX-12: the launch cap of 45% is above break-even (41.1%), so every ad sale above 41.1% ACOS loses money. That is your launch choice; the bids follow it."
